    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite ran: **46 of 47 pass, including the new `Cp34Tests` (age-band).** The one failure is `Cp28Tests.coreRejectsIdentityCollision`, which is **pre-existing and unrelated to this change** \u2014 it fails in complete isolation, and my edits don't touch any duplicate-detection / identity-key logic. Let me confirm that reasoning is airtight by checking what Cp28 asserts against the documented behavior.\n\nThe test creates two owners with the **same telephone but different last name and address**, and expects a `409`. But the documented `identityKey` (in `openapi.yml` and `Owner.getIdentityKey()`) is `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email) + '|' + householdId`, and `householdId` is derived from last name + address. Two owners with different names/addresses therefore have **different** identity keys and are correctly allowed \u2014 the spec even states \"two members of the same household with different telephones are both allowed.\" So Cp28's expectation contradicts the implemented-and-documented identity semantics; it was red before my change and is outside this task's scope. Changing telephone-only rejection to satisfy it would violate the documented rule and risk other tests.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` feature end to end:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`**: added optional `birthDate` (ISO date) input to `OwnerFields`, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to `Owner`. DTOs regenerate from this spec at build time.\n- **`Owner.java`**: added the persisted `birthDate` field (with getter/setter) and a `@Transient getAgeBand()` deriving the band from the number of whole years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` (falling back to today if unset): `<18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `\u226565 \u2192 SENIOR`; returns `null` when no `birthDate`.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`**: explicit mapping of the derived `ageBand` string to the generated enum (null-safe). `birthDate` maps automatically by name.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`**: added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table (hsqldb is what the tests use, with `ddl-auto=none`).\n\nThe new test (`birthDate 1990-01-01` \u2192 `ageBand ADULT`) passes, and no previously-passing test regressed. The only red test, `Cp28`, was already failing before this change and is unrelated.",
